[gd_resource type="Resource" script_class="Conversation" format=3]

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://game/dialogue/conversation.gd" id="1_convo"]

[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_convo")
id = &"lane_agnes"
text = "# DRAFT
# Agnes at the door of the Cross Keys at dusk, nights 1 to 6, while the abbey gate stands open.
# She carries the lane's talk of the turned away (before the bell they sleep at the Keys; after it the Keys is shut) and of the locked guesthouse.
# The Keys is open: an ale every night, and it ends the talk.
# Her own flags: lane_agnes_<night> (talked to her tonight), lane_agnes_n<night>_<topic> (asked).
== start
-> start_known [if talked_n0_agnes]
-> start_new

== start_known
Agnes: There's my lodger. They're feeding you over there, I hope?
-> tonight

== start_new
(A woman in the inn's doorway, shaking out a cloth.)
Agnes: You'll be the new porter. I'm Agnes. Hob's wife, God help me.
-> tonight

== again
-> back [if night=1] [if lane_agnes_1]
-> back [if night=2] [if lane_agnes_2]
-> back [if night=3] [if lane_agnes_3]
-> back [if night=4] [if lane_agnes_4]
-> back [if night=5] [if lane_agnes_5]
-> back [if night=6] [if lane_agnes_6]
-> hello

== hello
Agnes: Brother.
-> tonight

== back
Agnes: Back again? You'll wear out my step.
-> ask

== tonight
-> n1 [if night=1]
-> n2 [if night=2]
-> n3 [if night=3]
-> n4 [if night=4]
-> n5 [if night=5]
-> n6 [if night=6]

== ask
-> n1_ask [if night=1]
-> n2_ask [if night=2]
-> n3_ask [if night=3]
-> n4_ask [if night=4]
-> n5_ask [if night=5]
-> n6_ask [if night=6]

== ale
(She fetches a cup from inside and puts it into your hands.)
Agnes: The Keys is open, brother. Drink it slow.
-> end

# Night 1: nothing yet. The rule: send them to the Keys before the bell.
== n1 [set lane_agnes_1]
Agnes: Your room's still there if they turn you out. I've not let it.
Agnes: And if you've a soul to send away, send them across before the bell. After it, the door's barred to God himself.
-> n1_ask

== n1_ask
* [if not lane_agnes_n1_cell] They've given me a cell by the gate. -> n1_cell
* (Ask for an ale.) [drink] -> ale

== n1_cell [set lane_agnes_n1_cell]
Agnes: By the gate. You'll see who comes, then. Mind you see who goes, too.
-> n1_ask

# Night 2: about night 1. Where the merchant slept, if he was turned away.
== n2 [set lane_agnes_2]
-> n2_slept [if n1_merchant_fate=cross_keys]
-> n2_door [if n1_merchant_fate=lane]
-> n2_pond [if died_merchant]
-> n2_quiet

== n2_slept
Agnes: The merchant you turned away slept upstairs here. Grumbled all night. Better grumbling than in that place.
Agnes: Send them to us before the bell, brother, and there's always a bed.
-> n2_ask

== n2_door
Agnes: Your merchant came hammering on our door after the bell. Hob wouldn't unbar it. Rules are rules.
Agnes: He sat in our doorway till the light, cursing us. Lucky, Gib says. Send them before nine, brother.
-> n2_ask

== n2_pond
Agnes: That poor man in your pond. He had good fur on his cloak at your gate, Mab says. Did they bury him in it?
-> n2_ask

== n2_quiet
Agnes: A quiet night, for once. Hob says that's when to worry.
-> n2_ask

== n2_ask
* [if not lane_agnes_n2_jankin] (Ask her about Jankin.) -> n2_jankin
* (Ask for an ale.) [drink] -> ale

== n2_jankin [set lane_agnes_n2_jankin]
Agnes: Jankin? Hob puts him out at the bell, every night God sends. He's soft about everything but his rules.
Agnes: If you want Jankin kept in, ask Hob, not me. He might, for you.
-> n2_ask

# Night 3: about night 2. Someone turned away after the bell, killed in the lane; or Jankin.
== n3 [set lane_agnes_3]
-> n3_turned [if died_lane_death] [if lane_death_was_turned_away]
-> n3_jankin [if died_jankin]
-> n3_kept [if n2_jankin_kept_in]
-> n3_plain

== n3_turned
Agnes: Turned away after the bell, poor soul, and the Keys was shut. They found him in the gutter.
Agnes: Send them to us before nine, brother. Before nine, and we'll take them in.
-> n3_ask

== n3_jankin
Agnes: Hob hasn't said a word since they carried Jankin off. Not one.
(She looks back into the dark of the inn.)
-> n3_ask

== n3_kept
Agnes: Jankin's still asleep under my table. Hob kept him in, for you. Don't tell him I said it was kind.
-> n3_ask

== n3_plain
Agnes: The rain's stopped, at least. Small mercies.
-> n3_ask

== n3_ask
* [if not lane_agnes_n3_afraid] Are you afraid? -> n3_afraid
* (Ask for an ale.) [drink] -> ale

== n3_afraid [set lane_agnes_n3_afraid]
Agnes: Of course I'm afraid. I've a lane full of fools to feed. Being afraid doesn't bake the bread.
-> n3_ask

# Night 4: about night 3. A lodger who went in and wasn't seen again. Fog coming.
== n4 [set lane_agnes_4]
-> n4_pilgrim [if died_crypt_pilgrim]
-> n4_fog

== n4_pilgrim
Agnes: That pilgrim who lodged with us and went in at your gate. His bed's still made. I can't bring myself to strip it.
-> n4_fog

== n4_fog
Agnes: There's fog coming up off the river tonight. Keep your guests close, brother.
-> n4_ask

== n4_ask
* [if not lane_agnes_n4_bar] Do you lock your doors at night? -> n4_bar
* (Ask for an ale.) [drink] -> ale

== n4_bar [set lane_agnes_n4_bar]
Agnes: Lock them? I bar them, from the inside, every night. Hob has keys, and so did his father, and God knows who else.
Agnes: A key's only as good as the hands it's been in. A bar is mine.
-> n4_ask

# Night 5: about night 4. The guest killed behind a locked door, or the guest who barred it himself.
== n5 [set lane_agnes_5]
-> n5_guest_dead [if died_night4_guest]
-> n5_guest_lived [if n4_warned_night4_guest]
-> n5_rest

== n5_guest_dead
Agnes: They say the guesthouse door was locked, and it made no difference. Whoever goes in there has keys.
Agnes: If a guest of yours must stay, tell him to bar it from inside.
-> n5_rest

== n5_guest_lived
Agnes: Your guest last night barred his own door, he says, and sat up with a knife till dawn.
Agnes: He's gone home to Kent, and he won't be back.
-> n5_rest

== n5_rest
-> n5_edwin [if died_edwin]
-> n5_plain

== n5_edwin
Agnes: And a boy. They say a boy of yours was laid out in the bone house.
(She crosses herself.)
Agnes: God rest him. He was somebody's son.
-> n5_ask

== n5_plain
Agnes: You look worse every dusk, brother. Are you sleeping at all?
-> n5_ask

== n5_ask
* [if not lane_agnes_n5_pray] Pray for our dead. -> n5_pray
* (Ask for an ale.) [drink] -> ale

== n5_pray [set lane_agnes_n5_pray]
Agnes: I've prayed for your dead every night since Martinmas, brother. I'm running out of names.
-> n5_ask

# Night 6: snow.
== n6 [set lane_agnes_6]
Agnes: Snow.
(She pulls her shawl tight and looks at the abbey wall.)
Agnes: Whatever it is you've got in there, brother, keep your gate shut on it.
-> n6_ask

== n6_ask
* [if not lane_agnes_n6_what] What do you think it is? -> n6_what
* (Ask for an ale.) [drink] -> ale

== n6_what [set lane_agnes_n6_what]
Agnes: I don't think. I bake, and I bar the door, and I don't look out of that top window.
Agnes: You looked out of it, your first night. I saw your face in the morning.
-> n6_ask

== leave
Agnes: Before nine, mind!
"
